  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria Humanitarian Response Programme: UNHCR (United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to UNHCR Syria for Camp Management in Northeast Syria
This programme addresses critical gaps in camp management following the withdrawal of U.S. funding to Blumont, which left highly securitised camps such as Al Hol and Al Roj without adequate oversight. UNHCR will assume responsibility for camp management under a new operational strategy focused on sustainable solutions for camp residents. The UK will fund the camp management component of UNHCR&#x2019;s Syria Strategy, contributing to Output 3: Underserved Communities and complementing Save the Children&#x2019;s ongoing projects in the camps. The funding for camp management is a high UK  priority, with a Foreign Secretary steer that the UK should fund the new camp management model</narrative>
  </description>
